type: software
title: "Sharjah Criterion: A Two-Stage Empirical Lunar Crescent Visibility Model"
version: 1.1.0
date-released: "2026-11-25"
authors:
  - family-names: Talafha
    given-names: Mohammed
    email: mtalafha901@gmail.com
    affiliation: "Research Institute of Sciences and Engineering, University of Sharjah"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.20755359
repository-code: "https://github.com/mtalafha90/Sharjah_Criterion"
abstract: >
  A data-driven two-stage logistic-regression criterion for lunar crescent
  visibility, derived from the crescent sighting reports of the Islamic
  Crescents' Observation Project (ICOP). The pipeline
  scrapes, cleans, and enriches observations with astronomical features,
  trains stage-1 (detectability) and stage-2 (naked-eye vs. aided) models,
  selects operational thresholds, and validates externally against the
  Alrefay et al. (2018) published tables. The analysis scripts reproduce
  every table and figure of the accompanying paper, 'Sharjah criterion for
  lunar crescent visibility' (submitted to Astronomy and Computing).
keywords:
  - lunar crescent
  - crescent visibility
  - Islamic calendar
  - hilal
  - logistic regression
  - astronomical criterion
  - ICOP
  - Alrefay
